      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Are the problems bad enough to outweight the ammount of creators having all of their avatars hidden by a lot of people for unfair/unrealistic calculations? If creators get too frustrated, they will leave. That impacts the community in a very bad way. I know it's easier said than done, but the current method is, with all respects, bad. Even the previous method was less unfair.",
